# Dauthi Voidwalker comes down on turn 1 off a Mox Jet. On turn 3 Bot1 exiles Bot2's Ornithopter with Swords to
# Plowshares - an ordinary exile, so the card has no void counter - and then sacrifices Dauthi Voidwalker: there is no
# exiled card an opponent owns with a void counter on it, so the ability does nothing, and the Ornithopter (an
# opponent's exiled card without a counter) may not be cast. Nothing is asked.

